WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.140
A tourist is looking for the post office.

2
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.710
Przepraszam, jak dojść do poczty?

3
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.880
Proszę iść prosto, a potem w prawo.

4
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.230
A polite instruction: the polite word, then a verb.

5
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.240
Czy to daleko?

6
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.370
Nie, to blisko. Pięć minut.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.460
Dziękuję bardzo!

8
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.490
Proszę iść prosto.

9
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:37.530
Straight on, left, right, near and far are short and easy to catch.

10
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.160
Listen for them in the answer.

11
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.520
Adam is looking for the station. What does he ask?

12
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.640
Przepraszam, jak dojść do dworca?

13
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.000
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

14
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.920
Przepraszam, jak dojść do dworca?

15
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.240
He asks if it is far.

16
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.600
Czy to daleko?

17
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.960
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

18
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.120
Czy to daleko?

19
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.440
Ewa says it is near.

20
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.800
To jest blisko.

21
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.160
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

22
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.320
To jest blisko.

23
00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.880
